WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.256
A symmetric attack would be
highly escalatory

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.536
and unpredictable.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.976
Lieutenant Colonel Cavendish.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.040
deploy our response
to Russia's attack.

5
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.976
No-one else would use
your login on the sandbox?

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.376
And there were no Russian
connections? His gaming company?

7
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.976
Welcome. Russian coders.

8
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.256
You are here to re-design your
breaking and entering tool for us.

9
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.016
I'm done here with
recoding the search tool.

10
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.136
I've been monitoring you.

11
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.856
I love my country.
but my country is not CCP.

12
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.656
This is the address of
a friend in the movement.

13
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.856
LOUD BUZZER
Her name is Hai. Maybe she can help.

14
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.496
Not interrupting. am I?

15
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.576
I bet if you look in your files

16
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.856
you'll find me named as
a CCP spy in intercepted messages.

17
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.696
I only erased your files

18
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.696
because I believed in
what I thought you stood for.

19
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.976
You used to say you wanted
to do what is fair and just.

20
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.136
Now's your opportunity.

21
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.576
If this were to come to light.
you'd lose your job.

22
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.416
your husband -
his career would be destroyed.

23
00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.576
I thought you should
know first off -

24
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.880
Charlie's found the mole.

25
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.560
{\an8}ALARM BEEPS.

26
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.120
Oh. you're up.

27
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.136
Yeah. Heading to London.

28
00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.096
You didn't say you had anything.

29
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.136
Got a text late last night -
trade talks.

30
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.616
One of the PM's Special Advisers
wants an in-person briefing

31
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.680
on the security of
Chinese hedge funds.

32
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.256
Well. one of my team is
facing serious charges.

33
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.496
Well. I'm sorry to hear that...

34
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.176
I really need to be there.

35
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.640
Can't one of your colleagues go?

36
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.936
Can't you get one of yours?

37
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.496
I'm head of the China Team -

38
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.240
it's my job to report to government.

39
00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.256
You're going to have to
drop the kids for once.

40
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.080
Since when do we talk to
each other like this?

41
00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.296
Since I have to look after them

42
00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.800
while you're managing
one bloody crisis after another.

43
00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.880
What is this really about. Barbara?

44
00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.960
It's about me doing my job. Danny.

45
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:04.680
Hey.

46
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.096
Ah. Sorry. sorry.

47
00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.536
I had the kids and
Barbara got called away.

48
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.776
We were discussing
external agencies.

49
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.296
We can't be seen
to police ourselves.

50
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.776
Well. surely we're still
only questioning Phil.

51
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.336
Questioning officially now.

52
00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.136
Yeah. well. none of us
here think he's guilty.

53
00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.536
And I think that speaks directly
to the need for external auditing.

54
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.920
Now. if you don't mind. I am late.

55
00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.136
Sorry to interrupt. Danny.

56
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.416
Something's come up.

57
00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:42.936
Well. can Roz not take care of it?

58
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.136
She's not in yet.

59
00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.080
I thought the Army prided
itself on punctuality.

60
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.840
All right. I'll be there in a minute.

61
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.456
You all right. mate?
I'm fine. I'm just...

62
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.200
I'm late
and I'm already chasing my tail.

63
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.816
All right. Max.
what exactly am I looking at here?

64
00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.136
Well. it looks like
pretty simple code.

65
00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.696
And where has the malware come from?

66
00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.576
Department of Immigration and Visas.

67
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.376
It started turning
the printer on and off repeatedly.

68
00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.600
It caught fire.

69
00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.136
Well. what is it? Ransomware?

70
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.976
There's no ransom demand.

71
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.080
And Saara found this.

72
00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.216
The breaking and entering tool.
it's Russian.

73
00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.856
The same the FSB used
on its last attack?

74
00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.896
The same as the Russians used
in their recent attack

75
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.176
with modifications.

76
00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.216
So our definitive response to Russia

77
00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:43.496
led to escalation by them
or their allies within 12 hours.

78
00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.856
It could be a false flag.

79
00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.776
someone wanting us to assume that.

80
00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.376
This malware has not been
seen anywhere but here

81
00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.576
and wherever it was coded by the FSB.

82
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.816
And Shenzhen.

83
00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.936
Vadim said that's why they
were brought to China.

84
00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.240
to work on their malware for
the Chinese for APT10.

85
00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.560
Not a Russian strike after all.

86
00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.376
All right. Max.
let's just triage this

87
00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.776
and find out how it works
and what it's after.

88
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.816
Why don't I take the lead on this?

89
00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.016
Don't worry.
I won't blow up any shit.

90
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.240
unless I have to.

91
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.000
OK.

92
00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.456
Saara. any word from Vadim?

93
00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.576
Nothing.

94
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.816
Well. when he does get in touch.

95
00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.040
ask him if he knows anything
about this malware.

96
00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.296
TAPS KEYBOARD

97
00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.600
PHONE RINGS

98
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.696
Hi. Hi.

99
00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.856
I. um...

100
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.496
{\an8}I don't want to leave things
the way we did this morning.

101
00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.576
Yeah. sorry. it was early -

102
00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.336
I just needed that first coffee.

103
00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.000
So you're at Admiralty. then?

104
00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.496
The China trade talks.

105
00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.936
Yeah.

106
00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.136
Yeah. I'm just waiting
for them to break.

107
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.656
Barbara... 67!

108
00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.000
I got a 2:1!

109
00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.320
What's that?

110
00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.216
Don't know.

111
00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.536
Look. I think they're
calling us through.

112
00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.880
STAMMERING: I should go.

113
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.616
It's open!

114
00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.600
Nicky... Can I help you?

115
00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.096
Where's Nicky Chan?

116
00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.400
Never heard of him.

117
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.416
But this is his office.

118
00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.640
This is MY office.
has been for ten years.

119
00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.800
Oh. OK.

120
00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.840
Sorry. Sorry to bother you.

121
00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:23.576
KNOCKING

122
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.336
HEAVY METAL MUSIC IN HEADPHONES

123
00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.680
KNOCKING

124
00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.560
Hey. Victor.

125
00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:46.960
Victor Smith. exchange student. right?

126
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.776
Yeah. that's me.

127
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.816
How was your flight from Canada?

128
00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.216
Looks like it was shitty.

129
00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.840
Let's get you fixed up.

130
00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.536
Old bastard.

131
00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.336
telling tales on neighbours
for extra social credit.

132
00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.000
SHE SIGHS

133
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.936
You took your time. Russki.

134
00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.736
I expected you last night.

135
00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.296
I couldn't find it.

136
00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:25.336
I slept somewhere under a bridge.

137
00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.640
Liu says they're tearing
the place up looking for you.

138
00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.296
Liu's a friend of yours?
We have interests in common.

139
00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:35.800
He says they took your friend.
Misha? Took him where?

140
00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.936
Someplace he won't be
coming back. my guess -

141
00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.400
not in one piece anyway.

142
00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:43.976
He's got kids.

143
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.360
This is my fault.

144
00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.000
Listen. Russki...

145
00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.776
first rule. I don't want to know
what you've done. what you believe.

146
00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:53.880
No politics...

147
00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.120
strictly business.

148
00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.360
And he says you have friends.

149
00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.816
They're going to have
to come pick you up.

150
00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.576
It's too dangerous
for you out there -

151
00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.400
facial recognition.
and the MSS are looking for you.

152
00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.600
I don't know.
if I can message them...

153
00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:16.056
You can also tell them my help
costs 200.000 kuai

154
00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.200
in Bitcoin.

155
00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.656
Burners.

156
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.616
Tell them you'll message them back
in one hour on a new phone.

157
00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.880
Every new SIM costs them 2.000 kuai.

158
00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.120
Thank you.

159
00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.080
No thanks - Bitcoin.

160
00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:36.560
Now. clothes.

161
00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.656
You smell like under
a Shenzhen bridge.

162
00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.136
You shower.

163
00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.080
I'll take your clothes to
the laundry downstairs.

164
00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.560
WATER RUNS

165
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.536
My colleague Joanna from
Counter Intelligence will join me

166
00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:46.856
to audit questioning.

167
00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.136
I'll report to no-one until
we believe there are grounds

168
00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.376
for the DPP to press charges.

169
00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.520
I hope that allays
your fears. Danny.

170
00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.536
My fear is that
we have the wrong person.

171
00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.240
My hope is that you've
got the right one...

172
00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.216
or else the real mole
is out there.

173
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.656
as they have been for
the last 18 months. spying on you.

174
00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.160
DOOR OPENS

175
00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:09.936
Am I interrupting?

176
00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:10.976
No. we're just finishing.

177
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.656
Alex Sheldon. MI6 Chief.

178
00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.936
Roz Cavendish.

179
00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.600
Hm. Marston's girl.

180
00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.896
Lieutenant Colonel Cavendish.
Director of Rapid Reaction. GCHQ.

181
00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.360
And no longer a girl.

182
00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.936
CHARLIE: Right.

183
00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.896
shall we run over
a few of these details

184
00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.016
before we head down to Security?
Come on.

185
00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.056
Daniel?

186
00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.536
Before I'm consigned
to the dungeons.

187
00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.416
I might ask that lovely wife
of yours for a spot of lunch.

188
00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.136
Where would I find her?

189
00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.656
London.

190
00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:42.840
I'll tell her she missed you.

191
00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.560
I'm sure she'll be gutted.
DOOR OPENS.

192
00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.696
What's wrong?

193
00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:53.416
A senior management meeting
to which I wasn't invited.

194
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.696
It was a separate matter.
extremely delicate.

195
00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.416
You're just going to have
to trust me on that.

196
00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.776
That's the crux of the matter.
isn't it? Trust.

197
00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.656
You're in your hut. I'm in mine.

198
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:02.976
Did you have something to discuss?

199
00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.536
This new malware. it's propagating.

200
00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:06.776
Which suggests...? It's wormware.

201
00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.336
replicating itself to spread
to other computers.

202
00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:10.496
To what end?

203
00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:13.336
At the moment it seems
satisfied with internal chaos.

204
00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.656
Immigration was on the phone -
the whole system is at a standstill.

205
00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.656
We should be doing something
more than triaging.

206
00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:18.976
Step at a time.

207
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.456
Looks like we're
going to have to quarantine

208
00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.936
the whole Department of Immigration.

209
00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.496
I'll talk to the
Permanent Secretary...

210
00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.776
No. I will.

211
00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:25.936
That's my job.

212
00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.320
I said I'd call him back.

213
00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.000
And wasn't I to lead on this?

214
00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.720
And you've obviously got other
"delicate" matters to attend to.

215
00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.096
Hi. love. I just wanted to...

216
00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:58.696
VOICEMAIL: Hi. You've
reached Barbara's phone.

217
00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.280
I'm unable to take your call.

218
00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:16.136
It's Vadim on the secure line.
He's OK.

219
00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.656
He's confirmed this
attack was APT10.

220
00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:20.936
but he's stuck in Shenzhen.

221
00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.616
This is Danny Patrick.
Director of Operations. GCHQ.

222
00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:26.256
Vadim can stay here.

223
00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:28.496
but it costs. Mr Whoever You Are -

224
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.520
Bitcoin.

225
00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.056
Who is this?

226
00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:34.336
I'm Hai -
that's all you need to know.

227
00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:35.496
And you're with Vadim?

228
00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.456
Yeah. but MSS and State Police
are looking for him.

229
00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:42.096
OK. I can call MI6.
talk about getting you out of there.

230
00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.856
I'm sure we can arrange
a suitable fee.

231
00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.296
OK. as long as we understand.

232
00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.696
Vadim. Saara says you
and your colleagues

233
00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.656
were working on a breaking
and entering tool there. Yeah.

234
00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.776
Well. it's broken a worm
into our government system.

235
00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:56.056
Do you know what it's looking for?

236
00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.696
Not exactly. no.

237
00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.200
Saara says you have something.

238
00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:08.280
Vadim?

239
00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.936
I did get something -

240
00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.176
a long alphanumeric.

241
00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.816
Possibly a ciphertext.

242
00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:19.256
It was stolen from you in the
data scrape in the Russian attack.

243
00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.360
Can we have it?

244
00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:23.680
It could be really important to us.

245
00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:27.640
When I'm safe.

246
00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:32.416
Vadim. we're doing our best. really.

247
00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.456
And we could really do
with that ciphertext now.

248
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:35.976
I just spent a night under a bridge

249
00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.056
hiding from
the facial recognition cameras.

250
00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.840
If one of them spots me. I'm dead...

251
00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.456
so I could really do
with being safe now.

252
00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:46.336
I'll call back in one hour.
HANGS UP PHONE.

253
00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.560
We have to get him out.

254
00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:53.336
You're learning. Russki.

255
00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:56.000
Don't give anything away
in this world for free.

256
00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:06.256
We need Vadim Trusov.

257
00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.496
We've got an attack coming
out of China at present.

258
00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.136
and he holds the key.

259
00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.296
I'll see what we can do

260
00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:14.136
but. with the CCP love-in
going on at Admiralty.

261
00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.656
the Prime Minister
is going to resist

262
00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.040
exfiltrating a Russian citizen
from mainland China...

263
00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:21.440
at least until the trade talks
are concluded.

264
00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.440
Have your girl liaise
with our China desk.

265
00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.976
We'll get a plan in place
and ready to roll.

266
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.400
Alex. we really should begin.

267
00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.400
Thank you.

268
00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:46.320
Saara. I've got a number at MI6.

269
00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:04.336
ALEX CLEARS THROAT

270
00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:06.456
Alex Sheldon. MI6.

271
00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:11.136
Our MI6 colleagues are here
to offer an independent ear

272
00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.720
to our ongoing investigation.

273
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.600
Can you tell us the main reason...

274
00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:20.080
for doing the gaming design jobs?

275
00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:22.600
Uh. I enjoy it.

276
00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:24.800
Not for the money?

277
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:29.336
That too. but I wouldn't do it
if I didn't like it.

278
00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.880
I've got a job here.

279
00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.176
Last time we spoke.

280
00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:39.296
you said that you could earn much
more in the private sector

281
00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.696
than you do here -

282
00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.096
does that bother you?

283
00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.576
WHISPERS: Shit.

284
00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.136
I didn't mean it that way.

285
00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.200
I was just saying how it is.

286
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.720
Have you thought about leaving GCHQ?

287
00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.360
Yeah. it's crossed my mind. but...

288
00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:01.440
I believe in the mission.

289
00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:05.096
And aside from everything else.

290
00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.256
what the Russians have done -

291
00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.640
Ukraine. the malware attack here...

292
00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:13.936
I mean. you've lost the plot
if you think I'd work for them.

293
00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:18.640
Phil. have you ever heard of
a company called XXN Ventures?

294
00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:23.360
No. Xiangxin Corp?

295
00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.120
Xiangxin? The...

296
00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.560
China tech giant?

297
00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:34.816
You think I'm spying for China now?

298
00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.696
Now I'm a communist?

299
00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.376
Fuck's sake.

300
00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.656
XXN supplied the venture capital
for your friend's company

301
00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.976
to produce and develop the game.

302
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.376
XXN are a subsidiary
of Xiangxin Corp.

303
00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:53.720
and Xiangxin Corp have established
links to the ruling CCP.

304
00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:55.800
WHISPERS: Fuck.

305
00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.616
You weren't aware?

306
00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:01.096
Of course not.

307
00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.256
Trouble is.
how can you prove what you did

308
00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:06.616
and did not know?

309
00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:08.296
Because it's the truth.

310
00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:11.896
OK. let's leave motive
aside for one minute

311
00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.400
and move on to opportunity.

312
00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.600
Hi. You've reached Barbara's phone.
I'm unable to take your call.

313
00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.296
Shit. PHONE BEEPS.

314
00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:33.800
Hi. Um...

315
00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.816
I just wanted to talk.

316
00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.840
This morning was...

317
00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:44.376
wobbly. and felt like before -

318
00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:47.360
you know. just sudden trips
to London. and...

319
00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.520
{\an8}There's difficult things
happening here too.

320
00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:53.776
It doesn't matter.

321
00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:54.856
Um. I hope you have a good day.

322
00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.856
KNOCKING Come in.

323
00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.536
Department of Trade and Industry

324
00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.296
reporting similar issues
as Immigration.

325
00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:03.936
Well. did you quarantine Immigration
like we agreed? Yes.

326
00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:05.576
We produced a timeline.

327
00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:09.216
The worm jumped 600ths of
a second before the door closed.

328
00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:11.096
It knew it was being quarantined.

329
00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.016
It still presents as simple code.

330
00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:16.336
but we think the emerging pattern
suggests something more complex.

331
00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.736
And the chaos and destruction
are deceptions for a deeper goal.

332
00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:21.896
So. while we were trying
to contain it at Immigration.

333
00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:25.056
it attacked the Department of Trade
during the trade talks.

334
00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:26.240
Maybe that's its deeper goal.

335
00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:29.536
I'm going to have to warn
the Prime Minister's office.

336
00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:31.536
Quarantine Trade too?
It didn't work last time -

337
00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.520
no reason to believe
it's going to work this time.

338
00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.856
We're going to have to
shut down the system.

339
00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:39.376
both Immigration and Trade
and all related systems. Completely?

340
00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:41.576
That will bring
those departments to a halt.

341
00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:42.696
And much beyond.

342
00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:43.816
Every computer turned off.

343
00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.896
It will close our ports.
airports. customs.

344
00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.256
And the China trade talks
will have to be suspended.

345
00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.296
I'm going to need sign-off
from the top for that.

346
00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:51.376
In the meantime.

347
00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:53.720
you just look for any clues as
to what its target might be.

348
00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.976
INTERCOM: Your call
has been forwarded.

349
00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.176
David Neal's office.

350
00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.936
It's Danny Patrick.
I need to talk to David ASAP.

351
00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.336
He's in a meeting.
I'll see if I can get hold of him.

352
00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:08.880
I'll wait. Please hold.

353
00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:25.136
TAPS PHONE KEYPAD

354
00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.296
PHONE RINGS
Legal Clearance. Fran speaking.

355
00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.136
Hey. Fran. it's Danny Patrick here.

356
00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.416
Hi. Danny. how are you?

357
00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.416
Er. good-ish.

358
00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.856
{\an8}We're dealing with a
Category 1 attack.

359
00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:37.456
I'm going to need access to ANPR.

360
00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:39.056
and key surveillance systems.

361
00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.336
for the duration.

362
00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.776
Can your office sign that off?

363
00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.736
{\an8}Yeah. I'll give you
emergency access now.

364
00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:44.936
{\an8}Will you just send over
the documents?

365
00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.136
{\an8}Yeah. I'll send over the paperwork.

366
00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:47.760
Thanks. Fran. I owe you one.

367
00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:50.280
What the fuck?

368
00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:58.336
Sorry. Danny.

369
00:22:58.360 --> 00:22:59.776
I'm afraid I can't reach him
at the moment.

370
00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:00.800
Do you want to hold?

371
00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:03.856
Never mind. I'm going to
go to London.

372
00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:05.360
Just have him call me ASAP.

373
00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:23.240
MUFFLED TV CHATTER

374
00:24:30.760 --> 00:24:32.280
Is there someone here
I could speak to?

375
00:24:39.040 --> 00:24:40.040
Hello?

376
00:24:58.840 --> 00:25:00.416
I'm looking for Nicky Chan?

377
00:25:00.440 --> 00:25:01.760
Chan Chi Lam?

378
00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:07.200
I know he comes here -
we have photographs.

379
00:25:27.160 --> 00:25:28.376
Um...

380
00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:29.800
I'm looking for Nicky Chan...

381
00:25:31.040 --> 00:25:32.080
or Chan Chi Lam.

382
00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:34.656
I need to talk to him.

383
00:25:34.680 --> 00:25:36.296
There is no Chan Chi Lam here.

384
00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:38.040
This is a Chinese takeaway.

385
00:25:39.680 --> 00:25:41.240
But you know and I know that...

386
00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:44.120
this is a Chinese police station.

387
00:25:45.560 --> 00:25:47.216
The police station is
on the high street

388
00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:48.480
if you need the police.

389
00:25:50.320 --> 00:25:51.600
You know that's not what I mean.

390
00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.200
You know this is
an MSS overseas office.

391
00:26:08.840 --> 00:26:10.880
The talks.
What the hell is he doing there?

392
00:26:13.680 --> 00:26:14.720
Who do you work for?

393
00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:34.376
Is there anything you want to amend?

394
00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:35.480
Or add?

395
00:26:39.400 --> 00:26:41.616
Because this statement
makes very clear

396
00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:44.560
that you had motive and opportunity.

397
00:26:50.240 --> 00:26:54.096
But you have no proof that
I accepted money from the Chinese.

398
00:26:54.120 --> 00:26:55.960
and you won't. because...

399
00:26:57.360 --> 00:26:58.360
I didn't...

400
00:26:59.640 --> 00:27:00.776
not knowingly.

401
00:27:00.800 --> 00:27:03.216
You can't prove that I
accessed the MAC address

402
00:27:03.240 --> 00:27:04.480
at a specific time.

403
00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:07.496
I mean. your only hope
is that I confess.

404
00:27:07.520 --> 00:27:09.360
which I'm not going to do.
because...

405
00:27:10.360 --> 00:27:12.336
Because I didn't do anything. OK?

406
00:27:12.360 --> 00:27:13.736
Listen. Phil.

407
00:27:13.760 --> 00:27:16.896
you accessed the sandbox
on an almost daily basis

408
00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:18.616
when the MAC address was stolen.

409
00:27:18.640 --> 00:27:20.496
In the same period of time.

410
00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:24.096
you also accepted money
from a CCP proxy -

411
00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:25.720
Xiangxin Technology Corp.

412
00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:29.416
Nothing's ever lost.

413
00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:32.680
There will be a record somewhere
of who accessed the MAC address.

414
00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:36.776
DAVID: I've spoken to the PM's office

415
00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:38.376
and it's a no to shutting it down.

416
00:27:38.400 --> 00:27:41.336
They have introduced a worm
into the government system.

417
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:42.816
Every time we try and quarantine it.

418
00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:43.936
it jumps.

419
00:27:43.960 --> 00:27:45.656
It's looking for something.

420
00:27:45.680 --> 00:27:47.576
It could well be to
do with the talks.

421
00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:49.056
But what exactly?

422
00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:51.136
Well. we don't know!

423
00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:54.296
That's why we have to shut
the system down so we can find out.

424
00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:57.176
We can't argue that it
poses an immediate threat

425
00:27:57.200 --> 00:27:58.896
because we don't know
what that threat is.

426
00:27:58.920 --> 00:28:01.496
DANNY STAMMERS
When you identify that.

427
00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:02.536
we'll go back to them.

428
00:28:02.560 --> 00:28:04.976
PHONE RINGS
Understood. I've got to jump.

429
00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:06.336
Roz.

430
00:28:06.360 --> 00:28:07.696
Tell me you've got some good news.

431
00:28:07.720 --> 00:28:10.656
Yeah. I'm going to have
to disappoint you there.

432
00:28:10.680 --> 00:28:12.336
We passed it through
reverse engineering

433
00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:14.096
but they've used environment keying.

434
00:28:14.120 --> 00:28:15.680
You know Marston. right?

435
00:28:19.320 --> 00:28:21.176
Yes. a bit.

436
00:28:21.200 --> 00:28:23.296
All right. well. can you call him?

437
00:28:23.320 --> 00:28:25.296
As minister responsible
and Deputy PM.

438
00:28:25.320 --> 00:28:26.840
he might be able to authorise us.

439
00:28:28.320 --> 00:28:30.760
I'll see what I can do. Thank you.

440
00:28:39.440 --> 00:28:41.256
Mind if I have a word with Saara?

441
00:28:41.280 --> 00:28:43.296
Yes. in fact. I do.

442
00:28:43.320 --> 00:28:44.736
Wasn't really a question.

443
00:28:44.760 --> 00:28:46.080
Saara. we'll talk in here.

444
00:29:01.520 --> 00:29:03.536
So is he right?

445
00:29:03.560 --> 00:29:04.560
Phil?

446
00:29:05.680 --> 00:29:06.800
Is nothing ever lost?

447
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.080
Are you questioning him?

448
00:29:11.520 --> 00:29:13.856
I can't comment on
current inquiries.

449
00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:16.280
That's what people say in here
when they mean "yes".

450
00:29:21.080 --> 00:29:23.496
The files in the system settings
were cleaned out

451
00:29:23.520 --> 00:29:25.576
during the Russian attack
and Chinese data scrape.

452
00:29:25.600 --> 00:29:27.496
And there's no other way
to retrieve them?

453
00:29:27.520 --> 00:29:28.600
Not that I...

454
00:29:31.920 --> 00:29:33.320
Let me try something. What?

455
00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:37.736
{\an8}Start.

456
00:29:37.760 --> 00:29:39.576
{\an8}Control Panel.

457
00:29:39.600 --> 00:29:41.016
{\an8}Network and Internet.

458
00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:43.056
Network and Sharing Center.

459
00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:44.336
MAC Address Network.

460
00:29:44.360 --> 00:29:45.360
{\an8}Details.

461
00:29:47.720 --> 00:29:50.376
The keys you hit when you
access the MAC address.

462
00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:51.496
the pattern.

463
00:29:51.520 --> 00:29:52.560
maybe there's a trace.

464
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.120
Could you find them?

465
00:29:56.600 --> 00:29:57.736
Will it help Phil?

466
00:29:57.760 --> 00:29:59.400
I can't comment on that.

467
00:30:02.280 --> 00:30:06.136
We wouldn't be asking if we
did not think it was imperative.

468
00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:08.736
Danny Patrick put you up to this.
didn't he?

469
00:30:08.760 --> 00:30:09.920
This is his phone line.

470
00:30:10.960 --> 00:30:12.696
A moment. No. no. no. no.

471
00:30:12.720 --> 00:30:14.176
You can't take her.

472
00:30:14.200 --> 00:30:16.000
Internal security takes precedence.

473
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.336
Ah. this place.

474
00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:22.016
Richard...

475
00:30:22.040 --> 00:30:23.616
It's a no in any event. Roz.

476
00:30:23.640 --> 00:30:27.296
We are ratifying a trade deal
with the top Chinese delegation.

477
00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:30.296
We cannot have the lights at
the Department of Trade go out.

478
00:30:30.320 --> 00:30:31.736
End of.

479
00:30:31.760 --> 00:30:33.600
Your job is to keep them on. soldier.

480
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.520
TAPS PHONE KEYPAD

481
00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:45.120
It's a no from Marston.

482
00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:47.816
Why does that not surprise me?

483
00:30:47.840 --> 00:30:50.120
OK. Thank you for trying.
I appreciate it.

484
00:30:55.680 --> 00:30:56.680
Where are you going?

485
00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:02.296
PM Andrew Makinde and
Foreign Secretary Richard Marston

486
00:31:02.320 --> 00:31:04.296
reconvened their
landmark trade talks

487
00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:06.216
with China at Admiralty House today.

488
00:31:06.240 --> 00:31:08.736
The Government hail it as
a watershed moment.

489
00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:12.216
claiming the potential for
billions of pounds in economic gains.

490
00:31:12.240 --> 00:31:14.576
But the negotiations
are controversial.

491
00:31:14.600 --> 00:31:17.816
with critics warning that a deeper
strategic partnership with Beijing

492
00:31:17.840 --> 00:31:20.016
risks compromising British security.

493
00:31:20.040 --> 00:31:22.600
SIREN WAILS

494
00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:39.560
Sorry. excuse me.

495
00:31:42.760 --> 00:31:43.760
Pass?

496
00:31:50.560 --> 00:31:51.736
Not on the list.

497
00:31:51.760 --> 00:31:53.256
Oh. come on. I'm GCHQ.

498
00:31:53.280 --> 00:31:54.656
Please keep the entrance clear.

499
00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:56.600
Oh. come on. you've got to let...

500
00:32:18.840 --> 00:32:19.840
Right.

501
00:32:27.280 --> 00:32:32.216
So. the talks are progressing
extremely well. as I would've hoped.

502
00:32:32.240 --> 00:32:36.016
but I'm sure you can appreciate
these things do take some time.

503
00:32:36.040 --> 00:32:39.136
However. I hope that.
within the next 48 hours.

504
00:32:39.160 --> 00:32:41.376
we will have an agreement
on the table

505
00:32:41.400 --> 00:32:43.816
which both sides are satisfied with

506
00:32:43.840 --> 00:32:47.056
{\an8}and which will be of great benefit

507
00:32:47.080 --> 00:32:49.816
{\an8}to both the United Kingdom and China.

508
00:32:49.840 --> 00:32:52.280
MUFFLED CHATTER

509
00:33:32.280 --> 00:33:33.856
Barbara.

510
00:33:33.880 --> 00:33:35.496
What a nice surprise.

511
00:33:35.520 --> 00:33:36.736
It's been a while.

512
00:33:36.760 --> 00:33:37.880
It has indeed.

513
00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:41.680
Let's take a walk in St James's
Park. shall we. Nicky Chan?

